#set heading(numbering: none)

= Syllabus and Overview

#fade[Michaelmas Term, 2026] #h(1fr) #fade[[16 Lectures]]

*Physical Background* #h(1fr) #fade[[1 Lecture]]

Photoelectric effect. Electrons in atoms and line spectra. Particle diffraction.

*Schrödinger Equation and Solutions* #h(1fr) #fade[[6 Lectures]]

De Broglie waves. Schrödinger equation. Superposition principle. Probability interpretation, density and current. #h(1fr) #fade[[2]]

Stationary states. Free particle, Gaussian wave packet. Motion in 1-dimensional potentials, parity. Potential step, square well and barrier. Harmonic oscillator. #h(1fr) #fade[[4]]

*Observables and Expectation Values* #h(1fr) #fade[[4 Lectures]]

Position and momentum operators and expectation values. Canonical commutation relations. Uncertainty principle. #h(1fr) #fade[[2]]

Observables and Hermitian operators. Eigenvalues and eigenfunctions. Formula for expectation value. #h(1fr) #fade[[2]]

*Hydrogen Atom* #h(1fr) #fade[[5 Lectures]]

Spherically symmetric wave functions for spherical well and hydrogen atom.

Orbital angular momentum operators. General solution of hydrogen atom.
